iliary files `<Name>_Abs.tla` & `<Name>_Impl.tla` plus a refinement aux that EXTENDS them — and the parent file references `INSTANCE BoundedQueue_Impl WITH buffer <- buffer`, but the impl module declares its variable via PlusCal (which translates to `VARIABLES buffer, pc`). The INSTANCE substitution would require providing `pc` too — or the parent\'s variables must include pc, which they don\'t. That would cause a semantic error in the parent. But the per-module init/consec errors are about each module standalone — those failures cannot be caused by the parent.\\n\\nLet me look more carefully. The BoundedQueue (abs) is simple and pure. The issue might be that my modules use names like `BoundedQueue_Abs` in the MODULE header but the verifier expects just `BoundedQueue_Abs` matching the `name` field\'s <name>_Abs convention. That seems right. \\n\\nWait — the error says \\"Parsing or semantic analysis failed\\" but it\'s the same for all modules including abs. Maybe the verifier reads `tla_source` for impl modules and runs PlusCal translation on it; if PlusCal translation injects \\\\* BEGIN TRANSLATION markers, that\'s fine. But maybe my `tla_source` field for impls already contains usable PlusCal — but the spec says \\"Do NOT pre-insert `\\\\* BEGIN TRANSLATION`\\" — I didn\'t, good.\\n\\nMaybe the BoundedQueue_Abs module declares `CONSTANTS Capacity, MaxVal` but my constants config in the bundle attached the constants to the IMPL only, not the ABS. The verifier likely uses the same constants for both. Let me also attach constants to abs.\\n\\nActually re-reading the schema: `constants` is on each module item. The abs modules also have CONSTANTS but I didn\'t supply constants for them. That\'s probably the parse/semantic failure (TLC can\'t initialize without constant assignment). Let me add constants to every abs module too.', 'targeted_failure': 'all/parse', 'slug': 'producer_consumer_system', 'parent': {'name': 'ProducerConsumerSystem', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', '